{{!< default}}
{{!-- Template Name: About --}}

<div class="about-page">
  <div class="inner">

    <h1 class="ab-title">Hi, I’m <span class="kw"><img class="kw-face" src="{{asset 'images/avatar-nav.jpg'}}" alt="" width="48" height="48">Shashank</span>.<span class="ab-sub">Thanks for stopping by.</span></h1>

    <p class="ab-lede">I grew up in <span class="kw">{{> "icons/top"}}<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Channapatna">Channapatna</a></span>, a small town near Bengaluru known for its wooden toys, and I was the kind of kid who was happy spending time on his own. After school I went into engineering, mostly because that’s what most of us were expected to do, and in my second year I moved to <span class="kw">{{> "icons/tree"}}Bengaluru</span>. I’ve lived here ever since.</p>

  </div>

  <figure class="ab-photo">
    {{#if feature_image}}
    <img src="{{img_url feature_image size="l"}}"
         srcset="{{img_url feature_image size="m"}} 600w, {{img_url feature_image size="l"}} 1000w, {{img_url feature_image size="xl"}} 2000w"
         sizes="(max-width: 824px) calc(100vw - 36px), 760px"
         alt="Shashank R" width="1000" height="667" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
    {{else}}
    <img src="{{asset 'images/avatar.jpg'}}" alt="Shashank R" width="1080" height="1440" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
    {{/if}}
  </figure>

  <div class="inner">

    <div class="about-body">

      <p>It was during those college years that I first got curious about writing. I started reading more and signed up for a couple of online copywriting courses without any real idea of where it would lead. By the end of 2019, someone paid me to write for the first time, and I kept going from there.</p>

      <p>Marketing came into the picture soon after as an extension of writing, and I ended up enjoying it just as much. I worked across content and marketing roles and spent close to two years at <a href="https://www.thetesttribe.com/">The Test Tribe</a>, working on communities and events. Today I’m at <a href="https://www.growedin.com/">GrowedIn</a>, where I help executives and companies build their presence on LinkedIn in their own voice, which is the kind of work I had always wanted to do.</p>

      <p>Outside work, my life moves at a slower pace. I prefer a small circle over big crowds, and most of my weekends go into a movie, a show, or a long conversation with friends. Every now and then, it’s an <span class="kw">{{> "icons/ticket"}}arcade</span> or a game.</p>

      <p>This year, some of those weekends turned into trips. I went to <span class="kw">{{> "icons/boulders"}}<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hampi">Hampi</a></span> with my cousins, and to <span class="kw">{{> "icons/waves"}}<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kannur">Kannur</a></span> in Kerala and <span class="kw">{{> "icons/train"}}<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ooty">Ooty</a></span> with my friends. I also took <span class="kw">{{> "icons/plane"}}<a href="/my-first-flight-blr-amd/">my first flight</a></span> this year, something I had wanted to do since I was a kid watching planes at night.</p>

      <p>As for this site, it’s where I write for myself. I’m still a student when it comes to writing, and most of what I share here is me trying to understand something better, without any fixed schedule or pressure to be consistent.</p>

      <p>It took me longer than it should have to start this. I kept putting it off, thinking it needed more time, more planning. <a href="https://keyurkumbhare.com/">Keyur</a> kept pushing me for long enough that eventually I just started. Thanks to him. To my surprise, this site came together faster than I expected. Built using <a href="https://claude.ai/">Claude</a>, with <a href="https://ghost.org/">Ghost</a> and <a href="https://www.magicpages.co/">Magic Pages</a> handling the backend. Kept it simple, and close to how I wanted it to feel. This version went live on 19th April 2026. I’ll keep tweaking things as I go.</p>

      <p class="ab-close">Thanks for reading this far. You’re always welcome here.</p>

    </div>

